2 CONT Ikshvaku (Sanskrit: इक्ष्वाकु ‘sugar cane’[1], pāli: Okkāka) was the first king of the Ikshvaku dynasty and founder of the Solar Dynasty of Kshatriyas in Vedic civilization in ancient India.
2 CONT
