1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Laxman Kumara From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Lakshman Kumara Father	Duryodhana Mother	Bhanumati Born	Hastinapur Died	Kurukshetra Battle Field In the Hindu epic Mahabharata, Laxman Kumara or simply Laxman is 
2 CONC the son of Duryodhana.[1] He had a twin sister called Lakshmana who was kidnapped by Samba (Krishna's son).[2] Not much is known about Laxman in Mahabharata. Contents  [hide]  1 Vatsala 2 Death 3 References 4 External links [edit]
2 CONC Vatsala
2 CONT
2 CONT This story is not there in Mahabharata but is actually an Andhra folklore. It seems that Vatsala(Sashirekha), the daughter of Balarama is betrothed to Abhimanyu. So initially the marriage of Vatsala is to be performed with Abhiman
2 CONC yu but when Arjuna goes into exile Balarama's wife Revati says that Abhimanyu's father has no kingdom left and a prince without a kingdom may well be a commoner. Balarama thinks about it and feels that his wife is right and that h
2 CONC e is supposed to think about the welfare of his daughter breaks off the marriage with Abhimanyu. He arranges it instead with Duryodhana's son Laxman. When Abhimanyu comes to know about this he is annoyed and asks Krishna to interv
2 CONC ene. Krishna says he cannot do so but he should ask help from his step-brother Ghatotkacha who lives in Varnavat. Abhimanyu sets out to Varnavat and meets his brother telling him why he seeks his help. Ghatotkacha is furious at Ba
2 CONC larama because he wants to keep an alliance with the very people who were the cause of the Pandava’s misery. Meanwhile the marriage preparations take place at Balarama’s house. Ghatotkacha goes disguised as Vatsala to the marriage
2 CONC  ceremony. He frightens the hell out of Laxman who promptly faints. Laxman vows never to marry. The real Vatsala has been transported by Ghatotkacha to Varnavat where Abhimanyu awaits. The couple’s marriage is celebrated. When Dur
2 CONC yodhana learns that Abhimanyu has married Vatsala he is infuriated and thus his anger toward the Pandava’s is further fuelled.[3][4] [edit]Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Laxman is slain on the 13th day of the War by Abhimanyu. He decapitates Laxman using the Nagastra. [5][6]
