1 NAME VATSALA / SASHIREKHA /Abhimanyu/
2 GIVN VATSALA / SASHIREKHA
2 _MARNM Abhimanyu
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Sasirekha Parinayam (a folktale based on Mahabharata), Abhimanyu, the son of Arjuna, married another woman before his marriage to Uttarā. The woman was named Shashirekha/Vatsala, the daughter of Balarama.
2 CONT
2 CONT The tale narrates that Abhimanyu fell in love with Vatsala, but Vatsala's father wanted her to marry Laxmana Kumar, the son of Duryodhana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wanting to help his cousin, Ghatotkach took the form of Vatsala and injured Laxmana Kumar's arm. After the incident, Laxmana broke his marriage to Vatsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile, the real Vatsala was in a forest along with Abhimanyu where, they married.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, this a folktale and there is no mention of this in the original epic.
